A "fail-closed programmatic axiom audit" — in Lean: use `Lean.Environment` constants, filter by module, get types, run `Lean.collectAxioms`, print `#print axioms` lines, and `#eval` a check that fails (e.g. `throw`) if any disallowed axiom appears. Fail-closed means: if a declaration cannot be found/analyzed, it must be reported as failure rather than skipped.

